    blurb: "The vectored-thrust jet that hovers and lands vertically.",
    body: "The Harrier directs its jet exhaust through four rotating nozzles, letting it take off and land vertically or from very short strips. It proved a fixed-wing combat jet could operate without a conventional runway, a landmark in powered-lift flight.",
