    blurb: "The first widely successful rotary-wing aircraft.",
    body: "Juan de la Cierva's autogiro used a freely spinning, unpowered rotor for lift and a conventional propeller for thrust, letting it fly slowly and land in a short distance. It could not hover, but it solved the rotor problems that later made the practical helicopter possible.",
